      "updatedAt": "2026-10-20T12:00:00Z",
      "content": "Before leaving the dock, check the wind and current and agree who is on the bow. Approach slowly from downwind or down-current, whichever gives the boat more control. Keep the engine in neutral as the bow reaches the pickup; use the boathook to lift the pickup line, then lead it to the bow cleat. Keep hands clear of the line and confirm it is secure before shutting down."
